   "Recommended: Twitch changes often.": 1,
   "Redraws on every frame instead of 5 times a second. Slower.": 1,
   "Saved next to each part as «name.chat-overlay.mov» (or .mp4). It works even if the stream had no chat on screen: put it on the track above the video, at the start of the part, and place it where you want it. It begins together with the part and can run up to a second longer at the end.\nIt takes a while: a long part can take from minutes to hours to draw, depending on the type. Emotes and badges are fetched from Twitch, BTTV, FFZ and 7TV when it is drawn, so it needs internet.\nSize on disk for a very busy chat (3 messages a second, 400 x 1080): about 3.4 GB per hour with Animation, 28 GB with ProRes 4444, 0.4 GB with H.264.": 1,
