   "Tools": 1,
   "Tools folder": 2,
   "Transparent · Animation: QuickTime Animation with an alpha channel. Lossless, much smaller and faster to draw than ProRes, and read by Premiere Pro and After Effects.\nTransparent · ProRes 4444: the same idea with the codec almost every editor knows, but very big files. Use it if your editor does not read Animation.\nBlack background · H.264: small and quick, but not see-through. In the editor, set the clip's blend mode to Screen and the black disappears.": 1,
   "Twitch mutes copyrighted audio in a VOD. Those stretches are added to the .markers.json as «muted» markers (the plugin decides the color), so you can see them in Premiere. It needs the plugin file above to be on. The same stretches show in red on the Plan tab's timeline.": 1,
   "Twitch stream downloader engine": 1,
   "Update yt-dlp": 1,
   "Update yt-dlp now": 1,
   "Use this copy": 1,
   "Used by the «Download only selected clip» button in the Plan tab.": 1,
   "Used when you load a VOD. You can change it for each VOD on the Plan tab.": 1,
   "Uses TwitchDownloaderCLI, downloaded the first time. Saved next to each part as «name.chat.json». Inside the .json the message times count from the start of the VOD, not from the start of the part; the file's start/end say which stretch it covers.\nTwitchDownloader is MIT licensed (github.com/lay295/TwitchDownloader).": 1,
   "Uses the overlay settings below (type, look, size, text size, frame rate). The video is not touched. If «name.mp4» (or .mkv…) is next to the chat, the overlay takes its size and frame rate; if «name.markers.json» is there too, it is lined up to the fraction of a second. The result is saved next to the chat as «name.chat-overlay.mov» (or .mp4).": 1,
